  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A motorcyclist covers $99$ miles in $3$ hours at a constant rate.  What is the speed of the motorcyclist?",
  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $99,$ by the number of hours, $3.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{99}{3}=99\u00f73=33.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the motorcyclist is $33$ miles per hour.",
